What is international marriage?Marriage between people of different nationalitiesHere, I will mainly explain the marriage between Japanese and foreigners.
In terms of the ratio of international marriages, the number of cases where the husband is Japanese is 1, and the partner countries are China, the Philippines, and South Korea, and the cases where the wife is Japanese is 5,060, and the partner countries are Korean, American, and Chinese nationalities. The data is more.
Also, if you live in Japan with a foreign spouse, there are some precautions regarding your status of residence, so please check for a smooth marriage.
The following documents are required to complete the procedure for international marriage in Japan.
The Marriage Requirements Certificate is a certificate that proves that the person meets the marriage requirements in each country.
By the way, there are of course cases where a Japanese person needs a marriage requirement certificate when marrying a foreigner overseas, and it proves that the Japanese person has the marriage requirement according to Japanese law. You can get it at the ward, town, or village office, but depending on the country, it may not be accepted if it is issued by the city, ward, town, or village office, so it is a good idea to check in advance.
The biggest difference is that the certificate of singleness is just a certificate to prove that you are single, while the certificate of fulfillment of marriage requirements meets all the requirements (mainly age) that must be cleared for marriage. It is proved that you are.
It will be a substitute document. All documents will be submitted to the government office together with the marriage registration, so a Japanese translation is required according to the enforcement regulations of the Family Register Act.
In some cases, it is not uncommon for no person to have accepted an international marriage.
Especially if you want to stick to your marriage date, it is a good idea to consult in advance.
When you get married internationally, you can imagine problems with nationality.
Since pedigree is adopted in Japan, if one of the couples has Japanese nationality, the child will also be given Japanese nationality.
Since dual citizenship is prohibited by law in Japan, those who became dual citizens under the age of 20 became dual citizens by the age of 22, and those who became dual citizens over the age of 20 became dual citizens. You must choose one of your nationalities within two years from that point.
If the couple is based in Japan, the foreign spouse must obtain a status of residence (visa).
Since Japan has a status of residence system, as of 2021, you will be permitted to work in Japan by obtaining a status of residence that suits your activity from a total of 29 types of status of residence.
The requirement for this status of residence is that you are married to a Japanese person (in the case of a child, a Japanese child or a special adopted child). It is checked that there is something and that you have the resources to live in Japan.
Formal marriage = living together is the criteria for immigration.
Anyone can afford to live in Japan.
In addition, the status of residence of a foreign spouse is not limited to "Japanese spouse, etc."
However, few people will obtain a status of residence other than their Japanese spouse.
There are two major points of preferential treatment, the first isThere are no restrictions such as employment restrictionsIt is that.
(There are some jobs such as civil servants that cannot be taken by foreign nationals.)
Most other statuses of residence require a period of stay of 10 years or more, but Japanese spouses can apply for permanent residence within 3 years of marriage and 1 year or more of residence.
However, there are many things that must be different from marriage between Japanese people, and it is often difficult to get married due to improper procedures.
