"Management · management visa" is 1 visa which can work with Japanese status of residence. Previously, what was called "investment / management" was changed from the 2015 year 4 month 1 day to the status of residence "management · management".
The status of residence for a specific skill is one of the newly created work visas. Unlike the previous work visas, the scope of occupations has been expanded and the application conditions have been eased by expanding the scope of occupations and aiming for specialty and skills through "exams" rather than education or work experience.
An intra-company transfer job visa is a staff member of a business establishment located in a foreign country of a head office, a branch office or other public office or institution that has a business office in Japan, relocated to a place of business in Japan and transferred at the office , Visa related to activities equivalent to "technical / humanities knowledge / international business visa".
This is a visa for those who have been designated as highly qualified personnel with a status of residence for "specific activities" or who want to become highly skilled human resources in the future. The first is a visa that can be obtained by foreigners who have been certified as "professionals" for the first time.
It is a visa for those who have been designated advanced talent for the status of residence of "Specific Activities" and those who want to become advanced personnel from now on. The 2 number has the status of residence of 1, and 3 year has passed, it is 1 requirement, and it is possible to conduct almost all the activities recognized by the employment status of residence.
Cultural Activities Visa is an activity of conducting specialized research on academic or artistic activities without income or culture or art unique to Japan, or under the guidance of experts, to acquire it.
A research visa is a visa related to activities engaged in research that conducts research based on contracts with public and private organizations in Japan.
"Visitor visa" is a visa related to coverage and other coverage activities based on a contract with a foreign media agency.
"Religious visa" refers to visas related to missionary work and other religious activities conducted by religiousists who were dispatched to Japan by foreign religious groups. A visa that is required for religious activities in Japan, such as monks, bishops, priests, evangelists, pastors, monks, priests, etc dispatched by foreign religious groups.
"Art visa" is a work visa for artistic activities accompanying income done by the following people in Japan, also called artist visa.
"Professor visa" is a visa related to research, research guidance and education activities at Japanese universities or similar institutions and technical colleges.
