What is naturalization?
3 types are prescribed for naturalization, and there are "ordinary naturalization", "simple naturalization", and "naturalization". Each has different requirements.
Common naturalization Normally naturalization is a general foreigner, foreigners who are born in a foreign country and who are coming to Japan for work or study abroad apply.
"Continued for 5 years or more" does not apply if you have lived in Japan for 2 years, then for some reason abroad for 1 year, and have lived in Japan for 3 years.
Also, as a guide when leaving Japan, the number of days you leave Japan once is 3 month or more If becomes, it is not considered to be "continue".
Even if you are on a business trip, hospitalized for your family, or for any other reason, it seems difficult to consider the reason.
If you have a student visa, you must live in Japan as an international student for at least 2 years, and after graduation, you must live in Japan for at least 3 years with a work visa.
You can apply for naturalization even if the working period is 1 year.
You can apply for naturalization if you live in Japan for more than 3 years.
You must be at least 20 years old to apply for naturalization.
