Differences between naturalization and permanent residence-is there any advantages or disadvantages?Which is more difficult?
In this article, I will explain the difference between naturalization and permanent residence, and the advantages and disadvantages.Naturalization and permanent residence are common in that they can live in Japan for an unlimited period of time if permitted, but the content is very different.
If naturalization is permitted, you will withdraw from your home country's nationality, and once you withdraw from your nationality, it will be difficult to return to your original nationality. You will apply.
Now, let me explain the specific difference between naturalization and permanent residence.
In the case of naturalization: Since you will acquire Japanese nationality, you will not have to go through any procedures regarding your status of residence (visa).
For permanent residence: Remains foreign nationality.When you leave Japan, you will need to use your passport from your home country.
In the case of naturalization: You can obtain a Japanese family register by notifying the government office.
For permanent residence: No right to vote or eligibility for national elections.Suffrage is not permitted for local elections, except for some local governments.
In the case of naturalization : Does not apply .
4Which is better, naturalization or permanent residence?
If you are granted permanent residence, you will not only have the advantage of having no period of stay, but you will also have the advantage of increasing the degree of freedom and breadth of life in Japan because you will be able to get rid of work restrictions and get loans such as loans. ..You can also apply for permanent residence on an individual basis.
Based on the differences between the naturalization and permanent residence systems mentioned above, and the advantages and disadvantages of each, you should consider which application suits you and your family and make your choice.
