Background of "sham marriage" becoming a problem when applying for a "Japanese spouse, etc."
If you are a foreigner who is a spouse of a Japanese who has married a Japanese,Japanese spouse etc.I am in a position to apply for a visa, but the term "spouse" here formally refers to a person who is actually legally married to a Japanese person. , Refers to those who live together and live together as a married couple who live together and help each other.
In addition, in the crime of illegal acquisition of status of residence, etc. stipulated in the Immigration Control and Refuge (Article 70, Paragraph 1 of the same law), Those who apply for false information, obtain a status of residence (visa) illegally, and continue to land or stay in Japan shall be punished by imprisonment with work for not more than XNUMX years, imprisonment with work, or a fine of not more than XNUMX million yen, or their imprisonment.
like this"Japanese spouse etc.As a matter of course, "sham marriage" is "a fake marriage" because of the visa examination contents and the attitude toward false applications found in the provisions of the Immigration Control and Refuge Law.Japanese spouse etc.This is a reason for disapproval when applying for a visa.
Even if the period from encounter to marriage is one month, even if the two are separated in age, it is not necessarily unnatural for them to be attracted to each other rapidly and to get married as long as they are human beings.
Under these circumstances, the Immigration Bureau must carefully examine the question, "Are the foreigners applying for this visa and the Japanese spouse having a true marriage?"
Ingenuity in application to convince the Immigration Bureau that it is not a "sham marriage"
Then, what kind of measures can be taken to convince the Immigration Bureau that "our marriage is not a fake marriage. It is a marriage based on the true intention."
"Japanese spouse etc.The visa application documents for the visa application for "" include "2 to 3 snapshots".
What I would like the Immigration Bureau to understand from the existence of this photo is related to the above-mentioned "marriage truth" and "marital relationship is continuing", so as much as possible to convince this point. It would be very useful to submit a long-term snapshot of.
Due to privacy concerns, some messages and deliveries may not be known to the Immigration Bureau.
It may be an overstatement to say that it is normal, but when Japanese people get married in Japan, they often go to see each other's parents before getting married.
From such an idea, the fact that photos of greetings to each other's parents are submitted before getting married is one of the things that tends to judge that it is not a false marriage but a true marriage. It may be a reference.
