What about international marriage procedures, spouse visas, and children's nationalities?
This time, I will talk about what happens to the nationality of the child if he gets married internationally.
The idea of acquiring nationality through a blood relationship inherited from parents.
Another isParental pedigreeThe idea is to acquire the nationality of either the father or the mother.
Representative countries of adoption are the United States and Canada.
However, since pedigree is adopted in Japan, the child will have dual citizenship of the United States and Japan, and it will be necessary to select nationality in the future. .
◆ Article XNUMX of the Nationality Law
A.When the father or mother is a Japanese national at birth
Three.If you were born in Japan and your parents do not know each other, or if you do not have nationality
However, this does not mean that it can be obtained unconditionally, and there are some conditions.
Two.The legal mother-child relationship is caused by the fact of birth, so if the mother has Japanese nationality, the child will acquire Japanese nationality by birth.
Therefore, if the mother is a foreigner and the father is Japanese, the child will acquire Japanese nationality by birth if the parent is married or the father knows.
If you do not declare your intention to reserve nationality along with the birth registration within 3 months, you will lose your Japanese nationality as far back as you were born.
There are countries in the world where you can acquire the nationality of the other country by getting married.
When marrying a man in one of these countries, the woman acquires the nationality of that country.
When that happens, the woman Dual citizenship However, in the case of Japan, we do not recognize dual citizenship. , "Up to 22 years old" or "two years after becoming dual citizen" must be selected later.
The biggest problem for children due to the different nationalities of parents will be nationality.
Japan is not a country that recognizes dual citizenship, so its children will be forced to choose their nationality in the future. .
I mentioned that if a Japanese couple gives birth in the United States, they will also have American nationality, but what if an internationally married couple gives birth in a birth-oriented country?
Brazil also adopts jus soli, which means that the child will acquire Italian, Japanese and Brazilian nationalities.
◆ Selection of nationality
This is required by the current nationality law, which came into force since 1985.
There are two ways to select a foreign nationality: submitting a nationality withdrawal notification to the Legal Affairs Bureau and submitting a nationality selection notification to the foreign country.
If you become dual citizen before the age of 20 IsFrom that day to the age of 22You need to make a choice.
If you do not select your nationality by this deadline, the Minister of Justice will notify you in writing.If you leave it for more than a month, you will automatically lose your Japanese nationality.
I think the shortcut to understanding is to think about the customs, cultural differences, ways of thinking, and times of each country.
