What is the status of residence for a specific skill?
Specific skills are the new status of residence created in 2019 and 4 months.
Foreign human resources who want to use specific skills are required to pass the designated Japanese Language Proficiency Test and Skills Evaluation Test, but unlike other statuses of residence, they are not required to have educational background or work experience.
Companies (accepting institutions) that can use the status of residence of a specific skill must belong to the 14 designated industrial fields.
Many people think that a specific skill is a version with a lower hurdle to apply for other work-related status of residence, but not all jobs can use a specific skill visa.
