1 What is a permanent spouse visa?
A permanent resident's spouse visa is a person who has a permanent resident visa in Japan or was born in Japan as a spouse of a special permanent resident (hereinafter referred to as permanent resident, etc.) or as a child of a permanent resident, and wants to stay in Japan thereafter.
It is necessary to say that you are a person who has the status of a spouse such as a permanent resident.
In addition, the marriage must be legally valid and is not considered legally valid in the case of common-sex marriage or same-sex marriage.
● If you are a child of a permanent resident, etc.
① My father or mother lived in Japan with a permanent resident visa when I was born.
② It is necessary that the father died before he was born and that he had a permanent resident visa when he died.
In addition, the term "child" here means a real child, and an illegitimate child or a recognized illegitimate child is recognized as a child, but an adopted child is not included.
So, for example, if your mother gave birth in a foreign country and you were born in a foreign country, this requirement is not accepted.
