The visa application (application for status of residence) is classified according to the purpose of stay.
A Japanese visa such as a spouse or the like is a spouse (wife / husband) who married a Japanese, a child of a Japanese child or a special adopted child is the status of residence to live in Japan.
means that a spouse (wife / husband) who is married to a permanent resident or a special permanent resident (hereinafter referred to as "permanent resident, etc.") or a real child of a permanent resident, etc., lives in Japan.
Settlers Visa is delivered when the Minister of Justice considers special reasons and allows you to reside by designating a certain period of stay.
A short-term stay visa is a status of residence for a short-term stay (within 90 days) in Japan.This visa does not allow you to earn income or rewards.However, in the case of "short-term stay for the purpose of continuous job hunting" for international students, employment is permitted if you apply for permission for activities outside the qualifications. Details of short stay visa
