The address requirement is one of the conditions for the application for naturalization to be permitted.The content is stipulated in Article 5, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the Nationality Law.
Article 5, Paragraph 1, Item 1 of the Nationality Law stipulates that "you must have an address in Japan for at least 5 years" as an address requirement.
However, the period required for this address requirement is relaxed if the spouse of the naturalization applicant is Japanese or if the applicant or his / her parents are born in Japan, and as a general rule, the working period. It will be shortened without being asked (simple naturalization).
