What is a religious visa?
Specifically, it is a visa required for religious activities in Japan, such as monks, bishops, priests, evangelists, pastors, monks, priests, etc dispatched by foreign religious organizations.
A religious visa is sent to Japan by a foreign religious organization to conduct religious activities and corresponds to a case where a religious doctor aims to conduct missionary work in Japan.
Even if you are invited to a religious group headquartered in Japan, the applicant is currently belonging to a foreign religious group (whether or not you have a direct relationship with a religious group in Japan), In addition, if you have received a letter of recommendation or a letter of recommendation from the relevant organization, it will be a person dispatched from a foreign religious organization.
