In this column Frequently Asked Questions When Applying for Naturalization "Tax Payment Status" I will explain.
Article 5 of the Nationality Law, which stipulates the conditions for permitting naturalization applications, stipulates as follows.
The Minister of Justice may not permit the naturalization of a foreigner unless he / she meets the following conditions.
In this way, Article 5, Paragraph 1, Item 3 of the Nationality Law stipulates so-called behavioral requirements, and the content of these behavioral requirements is "Do you comply with Japanese law?"
If you do not pay taxes or pensions, you will be considered to be "not in compliance with the law" and there is a risk that you will be denied permission even if you apply for naturalization.Then, how many years will the possibility of disapproval of tax and pension delinquency increase?
Resident tax for the last year
Personal business tax for the last 2 years
Corporate business tax for the last two years
Consumption tax for the last 2 years
Employee pension(Qualified person)For the last year
Tax returns are not only filed by sole proprietors and self-employed people, but may also be required by office workers, part-time workers, and part-time workers. In a naturalization application, whether or not the final tax return is appropriate depends not only on the behavioral requirements but also on the livelihood requirements.
・ Part-time job or part-time job2 or more placesIf you are
If these people do not pay their taxes properly, their naturalization application may be denied.
If you have a tax delinquency, you cannot submit a tax certificate that has not been paid.After paying the unpaid amount in full, have the tax payment certificate issued with no unpaid amount and submit it to the Legal Affairs Bureau.
The point at the time of application is not to make a false application even if you make a mistake.If you are uncertain about your tax payment status or pension payment status, consult an administrative scrivener or legal bureau who is an expert.
