Pregnancy after 30: turn the desired into a real one. How will age change, will pregnancy after 30 years be successful
Over the past decade, the number of primigravid women aged "for 30" has doubled.
Physicians retain the fruit, which until recently had no chance of breathing. Not a hindrance and many chronic diseases of the future mother, which are typical for a woman who decided on a pregnancy after 30.
Doctors agree: a couple who wants to have children should begin the examination in a specialized clinic as early as possible. If necessary, you can manage to treat diseases that interfere with fertilization and bearing, because the older people become, the lower the chance of conception of a healthy child.
• optimal structure of the endometrium for embryo implantation.
The disadvantage of at least one of these factors makes pregnancy after 30 impossible. The task of physicians is to identify the missing stage and have time to carry out its correction-treatment.
Many studies have confirmed the fact that, since 30 years, the genital functions of the female body are being suppressed. This is due to a number of factors.
With age, the woman's ability to conceive is reduced due to gynecological chronic diseases (endometriosis, fibroids, inflammatory processes), a decrease in blood flow to the reproductive organs, and resistance to uterine hormones. As a result, complications with implantation of the embryo and miscarriage of pregnancy.
The probability of its occurrence to 35 years is doubled. As a result of diabetes, the risk of premature birth, pre-eclampsia, diabetic fetopathy, complications of the placenta and stillbirth is greatly increased.
Pregnancy after 30 years is associated with an increase in the probability of miscarriage to 17 percent. This happens not only with the inevitable age-related changes in the body as a whole - miscarriages are caused by aging of eggs, which lead to genetic disorders incompatible with fetal growth.
A woman who has decided to become pregnant after 30 years, reduces the likelihood of natural delivery at 26%. By 35-40 years up to 40% of pregnant women are forced to go to cesarean section.
A significant decrease in tissue elasticity is characteristic, which leads to the risk of ruptures in the birth canal and bleeding. Placental problems, much weaker labor activity - all this is in most cases inherent in "age".
Problems with presentation, chronic placental insufficiency and premature detachment are what an older woman should prepare for. Pathological conditions of the placenta often lead to the birth of a child with low weight, intrauterine hypoxia, as well as to complicated and premature birth.
Full readiness for twins, triple. Researchers have proved that the age of a woman from 35 to 39 years greatly increases the probability of twin births.
Planning a pregnancy after 30, you need prepare physically, giving the body more time. Very beneficial in terms of relaxation and psychological support of yoga or swimming, meditation.
Pregnancy and childbirth will force the body to mobilize, use all reserves and forces to the remainder. Therefore, in order to facilitate his task and to protect the child, one should not be lazy and do not save, and pass Complete examination to exclude:
• diseases of the genital organs and inflammatory processes in them.
During pregnancy, pregnant women after 30 years necessarily carry out several diagnoses of congenital malformations and prevent fetal development anomalies. Blood from the vein for the determination of genetic pathologies is taken from 16 for 20 a week.
The professional approach of doctors and the consciousness of the future mother will lead to a healthy pregnancy and reduce the risk of complications.
They carried out all the tests, prepared for the maximum, recovered from everything that was, and what was not, and the pregnancy does not come. Many couples drop their hands.
With IVF, pregnancy is more often accompanied by complications: embryo implantation, ectopic pregnancy, premature interruption, and many others. Usually pathologies are caused by the condition of the patient, when the functions of the organs are lost with age.
Parents who decide on in vitro fertilization, you need to be ready for multiple pregnancies. This is a very frequent "side phenomenon".
We give birth to ourselves?
The issue of delivery is very important for pregnant women after 30, is it possible to give birth, or is it necessary to have a cesarean?
At 38 week, the expectant mother "aged" is put in the hospital and the date and method of delivery are chosen. The hospital will be offered to use programmed delivery with the help of injections of hormones provoking generic activity.
Therefore, a woman can safely decide on the first, or the next pregnancy, because she already has life experience, welfare, she has something to share with her little "miracle" - it's time to learn the joy of motherhood!
