Appeared relatively recently activated carbon diet causes heated debate specialists. Many doctors refuse to believe in the dietary properties of coal.
Like any medicine, activated charcoal has its pluses and minuses. In medicine, its main property - the absorption of harmful substances accumulating in the intestine has long been used.
Coal is also considered an antidote. It can act as an antidote, neutralize poisons and toxins from the gastrointestinal tract, until they begin to be absorbed.
The biggest problem caused by the uncontrolled reception at home of activated charcoal is its overdose, for example, with diarrhea. It seems that one tablet can not help, so we drink at least a few pieces, after a couple of hours drinking a handful to fix the result.
Uncontrolled reception of activated carbon is dangerous for the heart muscle - it removes potassium and magnesium necessary for its normal work from the body. And along with them, we lose calcium, which is often in short supply and is filled with great difficulty.
Mortally dangerous can be the reception of activated charcoal and with peptic ulcer and stomach ulcer - getting into the blood through damaged blood vessels, it provokes blockage and threatens with thrombosis. With ulcerative colitis threatens toxic dilatation of the colon, and this is a dangerous complication of such a disease.
Studies have shown that charring of materials for the production of activated carbon produces polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons - PAH, which can damage the genotype and cause cancer. For this reason, products with activated carbon should be used with caution.
