22 rare photos of Marilyn Monroe, which the photographer published shortly before her death
Among the legendary figures of the last century, the name Marilyn Monroe comes to mind one of the first. Charming blonde, which became the sex symbol of 50, was remembered all over the world for many years.
She knew exactly what she wanted from life, and received everything as a winner.
Some do not stand the burden of glory, others get tired of crazy fans, someone suffers because of love dramas.
It seems that the circumstances of the death of the actress influenced her image of beauty with a tragic fate.
It remains only to enjoy her playing in such cult films as "Gentlemen prefer blondes","Some Like It Hot","Unwanted"And her photographs.
It was this woman who best experienced the femininity and grace of the beauty, catching them with the lens of her camera.
In 1946, Eve started to take photos. In just two years she worked as a photojournalist in the well-known journal "Harper's Bazaar", And in 1957, she became the first woman in the agency Magnum Photos.
Most of the pictures from his personal archive were presented by the photographer to the general public at 2005 in London, where she moved shortly before Marilyn's death.
Sometimes we forget that behind every impressive photo is a great photographer, every brilliant film is the result of the work of the whole team, not just one Luc Besson or Steven Spielberg, and over every tremendous novel was spent not only one night not only a writer, but also a literary editor. Our memory is arranged so that we remember only the brightest moments of life.
