This combination of ingredients in the composition makes it possible to use the St. John's wort as a medicine for various diseases.
In nature, there are several varieties of St. John's wort, but for medicinal purposes a species of St. John's wort is used. The plant has such useful properties:
St. John's wort is appropriate to be treated in such cases: 1.
Treatment of diseases and removal of gum inflammation, healing of stomatitis.
The plant is suitable for the treatment of tuberculosis. The substances in the composition act in a complex way on the body, provoking expectoration of sputum, relieving inflammation and increasing immunity.
Patients after operations related to transplantation of any organ should not take St. John's wort.
The herb is incompatible with female contraceptive pills, as it weakens their effect.
With caution, you should combine the reception of St. John's wort with other antidepressants. This is especially true for the elderly and those who already have serious mental disorders.
