Writer and blogger Sandy Schwartz, who writes about the upbringing of children, cites as evidence the study of American psychologists. Parental love and care have a positive impact on the entire life of the child and form a lasting and happy relationship between the parents and the child.
Why the happiest and most successful children come from loving parents
The data of Child Trends, a leading US research organization focused on improving the prospects and quality of life of children, youth and their families, confirm that the warmth and love shown by parents bear fruit throughout the life of their child. But if there were no affectionate parents, the child, most likely, will form a low self-esteem; he will experience feelings of alienation, hostility, aggressiveness and antisociality.
In 2010, researchers at the Duke University School of Medicine found that children of affectionate and considerate mothers grow up happier, more stable and less anxious adults.
Psychologists ranked the mother's affection and attention on an 5-scale scale - from "negative" to "obsessive." About 10% of mothers showed a low level of attachment, 85% - the normal level, and about 6% - high.
Oxytocin is a chemical substance in the brain produced at the time when a person feels love and affection. It was also proven that he was involved in the process of forming a bond between parents and children, creating a sense of trust and support between them.
When you tell him what he did wrong, put a hand on his shoulder and hug at the end of the conversation. Children should understand: even if you are unhappy with their behavior, you still love them.
