Macadamia nut: health benefits and harms. What more?
The benefits of such nuts are that they:
treat inflammation of the internal organs;
gives the face a healthy and fresh look;
nourishes dry and dull hair, making them soft and shiny;
Despite the high calorie content, nuts can be included in the diet for weight loss. It is enough for overweight women to use 7-10 nuts per day.
Macadamia Nuts contain B vitamins and Omega-3. They affect the male body as follows:
Macadam nuts may only be given to children from 3 years old. During the period of active growth, the product fills the body with minerals, vitamins, micro and macrocells.
energizes the child for the whole day;
The product can be crushed into porridge or dessert. Nuts can not be abused, since an excessive amount of macadamia can provoke an allergy and digestive upset in the baby.
Due to its unique properties, nuts are also in demand in cosmetology. Macadamian oil is taken as a basis, which can be used as an independent product or as part of various cosmetic products.
Shampoos, balms and serums make it easy to comb your hair, make it smooth and silky. At the same time, the curls become less brittle and acquire a natural shine.
Also, caution should be exercised for those who manifest inflammatory processes in the gastrointestinal tract. If the doctor has prescribed a diet with reduced fat intake, you should abstain from nuts.
