Cats are not just amazing animals, they improve health and provide emotional support. Their ability to treat people is seen in the Ancient Egypt.
Modern scientific studies show that pet owners live longer than people without pets. They have a complex effect on a person: at the tactile and bioenergetic level.
It is scientifically proven that the presence of cats in the house favorably affects the mental and physical health of their owners. Contact therapy with their participation is a separate section of traditional medicine - “felinotherapy” (from lat.
Listening to the sounds of meowing, purring cats and watching them play are effective healing methods.
According to American studies, the risk of heart attack in cat owners is 40% lower compared to people who do not live with a feline. When interacting with an animal, blood pressure also drops: after 20 minutes spent with the pet, the heart rate decreases, and the blood pressure stabilizes;
Happiness and joy radiating to pets is a natural immunity enhancer. These animals feel when a person is sick and close by to provide warmth and comfort.
The vibrational sound of purring is in the frequency range from 20 to 150 hertz, which in medicine corresponds to ultrasound and is considered useful for improving tissue regeneration, compaction, and bone fusion. Animals with injuries often purify intensely to recover.
Feline therapy is also gaining popularity in the mental health field. It improves a person's quality of life and creates a special bond with his pet.
Cats are sources of love and affection. Upon contact with animals, the release of hormones of happiness - serotonin and dopamine - brings a feeling of euphoria and improves the immune system.
These home healers take care of the physical and mental health of the owner, give him a lot of love, warmth and affection. They are a source of endless happiness healing every member of the family.
