What can you eat nursing mothers in the first month after childbirth
Nursing mother's nutrition in the first month after childbirth- the guarantee of the health of the baby, so all women tend to ensure that their meals were right and useful for the child. What foods in the mother's diet will benefit the baby?
Necessarily in the nursing mother's menu in the first month after birth and not only should there be fruits and vegetables. Preference should be given to those that are grown in your region in natural conditions.
In the first month of a nursing mother, one should not eat foods that can cause allergies and dysbiosis in infants. Allergens include oranges, strawberries, honey, chocolate, crabs, mackerel.
Products that can be eaten by a nursing mother in the first month after birth should be fresh and healthy, and her menu balanced and varied.
