Why is a long scream dangerous?
Why are children crying?
Hunger is one of the most common reasons why children cry. The younger the child, the greater the likelihood that he will scream.
Especially in the first months of life, children should be fed at shorter intervals. At large intervals, children take a very large amount of food at once - and this often burdens the small stomach.
A newborn never screams because of malice or “vagaries”. The kid needs confidence that he gets feedback when he is afraid or in pain.
Often parents come, take the baby in their arms, give a pacifier and change the diaper. To avoid this stressful situation, it is recommended that you remain calm and look at the child for 3 minutes or talk to him calmly.
If the newborn does not calm down this way, soft and slow touches often help relieve stress.
Singing can calm children
According to scientific work, singing was much more soothing to children than gentle speech.
If the newborn cries for a long time and does not calm down, despite the actions of the parents, it is recommended to consult a pediatrician. Sometimes the baby screams due to physical illnesses that cause pain.
