Back in the early nineties, beekeepers noticed this strange phenomenon, and in 2006 it was already named "a syndrome of destruction of bee colonies." Scientists can not explain, why it happens and what it is connected with.
tell you, than mankind is threatened with the disappearance of bees and how you can change the situation. Everything is more serious than you think ...
Few people think about it, but about 30% of all our food requires pollination by insects, namely honey bees. These little hard workers are the glue of agricultural culture.
If bees disappear, people will also have a hard time. British zoologist, writer and TV host sir David Attenborough recently wrote on his Facebook page: "If bees had disappeared from the face of the Earth, people would have lived no longer than four years."
Having lost bees, we will lose one of the most useful and universal products on the planet - honey.
But this is far from being so effective, and this process is very slow. It will only help a little to compensate for the loss of bees, but does not replace it.
Yes, because cows, sheep and goats for normal life require alfalfa and other plants that pollinate bees. The variety of food will be reduced.
The lack of certain foods in the person's diet will lead to health problems. Studies show that the products pollinated by bees give us calcium, iron and a number of vitamins.
Just mix two tablespoons of ordinary sugar with one tablespoon of clean water and put it somewhere in the yard. It seems that this is insignificant, but if it makes at least one third of the world's population, many bees will be saved.
