How long can I sit at the computer?
How much can you sit at the computer for adults and children?
How much you can sit at the computer and why it's dangerous
It's unlikely that they think of their existence without monitors, tablets and the virtual world. And if some people work with computers, others spend in virtuality free all the time, playing for hours or communicating.
Of course, manufacturers are seriously engaged in protecting screens to reduce the power of radiation from the monitor. But what to do with other parts of the monitor, as well as the system unit?
Do not rely on the safety of laptops: they radiate, and how!
The skull bones are more delicate, and the brain substance has more conductivity. Hence the harm that the computer (or rather, the radiation) can cause at the stage of embryonic development, from miscarriage to fetal pathology.
Yes, the obvious harmful flicker, which the first monitors have sinned, is not today and the load on the eyes is akin to that given by a conventional TV. But the uncontrolled stay of a monitor over a period of time is fraught with an overstrain of the optic nerve, a decrease in vision, and the development of myopia-myopia.
The question of how much you can sit at the computer, directly relates to the development of varicose veins, scoliosis and osteochondrosis. If an adult or a child is sitting in front of the monitor for hours, blood circulation in the pelvic organs will be disturbed.
Closure, lack of interests and friends in the real world, sociopathy, shattered nervous system - such is the payoff for the time spent at the monitor. At adults on a background of full immersing in the virtual world insomnia often develops, that interferes with high-grade work and rest.
It is easy to understand that the question as to how much you can sit at the computer, and the answer arises: the less, the better. However, there are specific medical recommendations, according to which you should plan your work and leisure.
• work for a monitor for no more than two hours in a row;
• After two hours of operation, be sure to interrupt for at least twenty minutes. To interrupt is to get up, walk, do exercises to disperse blood in the legs and pelvic region;
How much you can sit at the computer, depends primarily on the age of the child. Until he was five years old, he could not be allowed to be monitored.
• Children from ten to 14 years can work for about an hour, making a mandatory break every twenty minutes;
If the computer clearly has a detrimental effect on the health of the child, you need to exclude it from the life of the student.
Adults often ignore the recommendation for active rest from working at the computer, but in vain. Just distracting from the monitor is not enough: in order to minimize harm to one's health, one must walk, ideally to take a short walk in the open air.
• looking out of the window, looking first at the point in it, and then, without changing the position of the head, to look further beyond the glass, on the subject in the long run. Work with focus close-away several times.
