When we paint a child’s misconduct in all colors, we exclaim: “How can this be?
”, We want to teach him to be responsible for his actions. The child is still learning to distinguish good from bad, and adults help him in this.
The child has to apologize, but does nothing to correct his mistakes. He is consumed by a sense of guilt, shame and his own worthlessness.
Everyone considers me guilty!
The result of this self-flagellation can be not only additional errors due to the transfer of attention to internal emotional discomfort, but also dismissal at will with a persistent conviction "I did not live up to trust!"
How could you strike Varya!
