Today Ernst Moro called a Slovenian medic. However, he came to the world as a subject of the Austro-Hungarian Empire in the city, which was then called Laibach, and today is called Ljubljana.
In 1899, the Austrian received a doctorate in medicine, in 1906 became a pediatric specialist, and a few years later Heidelberg University gave him a professorship. Throughout his life, Moreau worked on solving the extremely acute problem of infant mortality in those times and achieved impressive success!
