Photo by Maharaja Ram Singh II
Maharaja Ram Singh II rules in the Indian principality of Jaipur in the middle of the century before last. Today the time of his reign is considered in those lands a golden age.
Among other things, Ram Singh made a truly unique gift to the historians of the future. Prince-photographer, as his contemporaries called it, spent a lot of time capturing the culture of his kingdom in the ages!
Most of the pictures Indian ruler made between 1857 and 1864 years. The collection of glass negatives ruler for more than a century lay untouched in one of the wings of his palace.
The solicitors, advisers and guests of Rama Singh knew perfectly well about the preferences of the prince-photographer and willingly posed for him. It is difficult to say whether they themselves received the pleasure of it, but who at that time would refuse to fulfill the whim of the all-powerful lord?
Of course, Ram Singh never missed a chance to show the world the power of his soldiers. The pictures below were taken by the ruler in 1858 year.
The gift of the prince-photographer passed through the ages turned into a part of the country's cultural heritage. Scientists are happy, because thanks to these cadres, they had a unique opportunity to learn directly about the life of the Indian nobility of the past!
