How to overcome self-doubt?
Parents sometimes can not resist and project their dreams of success, happiness or wealth to children: where they have failed, their children will certainly succeed. By themselves, dreams have nothing wrong, but the stubborn desire of parents to try them on a child can sometimes reach such proportions that nothing is left of the child's desires.
If parents are too cared for
If parents constantly struggle with imaginary dangers, their children will most likely learn this distrust of peace and the fear of everything and everyone. The child begins to avoid any activity, especially associated with emotional or physical risks.
If the parents did not support
As a result, after becoming an adult, Maria never dared to enter the institute, even in the evening department, or quit her job, boring and not bringing moral or material satisfaction. Our internal ideas about how life should be arranged force us to change, grow and look for ways for development, but to build these ideas, parents are needed who will believe in us, will encourage us to listen to their desires.
She is talented, clever, and even beautiful, "says the proud mother, introducing her daughter to friends. A little frightened girl at this moment wants only one thing: to fall through the earth!
In order to gain self-confidence, it is important to understand that everything inevitably collides with failures and failures, but it depends on us whether we will be able to extract from this some experience or fall into the abyss of self-abasement and self-doubt. First, none of the life lessons can be unambiguously negative.
