Acne in adolescence is a normal occurrence, which It is relatively common in the modern world. However, many people older than 30 years still suffer from acne.
Similar changes in adulthood can be caused by external factors - regular contact with oils, tar or chlorine. Therefore, the so-called "professional acne" occurs, which is more common on the hands and face.
In combination with exposure to the sun, acne sometimes occurs on the face, décolleté, shoulders and back. According to the expert, the disorder is called Mallorca's acne and is accompanied by an irritating, itchy rash.
Hormonal fluctuations can be caused, for example, by pregnancy, discontinuation of birth control pills or drugs. Medications include cortisone and antidepressants.
A natural remedy often helps with acne: from plant components on healing earth and zinc ointment to relaxation methods to relieve stress. However, it is recommended to first find out the cause of acne before acting independently against skin irritation.
Acne disappears by 20 years, although sometimes it persists in adulthood. It is possible that some scars remain permanent.
