Teething in children.
Especially if it's about dental health. The nature of the appearance of milk teeth, their further replacement by constant, is an important point of the child's physical development.
The cut out milk teeth are tightly pressed together, there are no gaps or crevices between them. But, to approach the time of changing milk teeth to permanent teeth, the spaces between the teeth should appear.
Previously there was such an assumption that the later appearance of teeth in children is caused by a disease such as rickets. But after numerous studies, scientists came to the conclusion that this assumption is erroneous.
If the teeth are about to crawl, his gums will be reddened and slightly swollen. This is explained by the increased blood supply of this part of the oral mucosa.
There are several other ways that a child can be helped in this situation:
