After giving birth, the peasant women were given vodka, and the noble women were given coffee
It is believed that pregnant and newly born women were treated with reverence. This is partly true, but if you study the issue in more detail, it becomes clear that not everything is as rosy as it seems at first glance.
Often, they sent for a priest, since childbirth could end in the death of both the mother and the child. If the last did not go away, then the woman stuck her hair in her mouth.
As for the umbilical cord, it was bandaged with linen thread, and in some regions it was cut. Next, the midwife smoothed the arms, legs, massaged the tummy, and also washed the body of the newborn in a special solution.
But women suffered this in the first three days after the birth of the baby. No one thought that from overheating, a woman in labor could open up bleeding, it was believed that a bath is a guarantee of health and it is impossible to take off from it.
The noblemen drank coffee and fed white bread. What are colic, allergies or anxiety?
In general, newborn children were handed over to peasant women. Yes, yes, thereby recently drinking vodka after childbirth.
With lure in the old days did not drag. What for?
Products were given from 2 for a week old, only in some provinces they waited 2 for months. Caring women prepared delicious porridge from milk and millet.
Cough is one of the most important clinical signs of bronchial asthma. In this disease, cough can be the equivalent of attacks of suffocation.
Coughing in a child can also be caused by diseases not associated with the respiratory system. For example, it can occur in children with heart defects or gastrointestinal pathology.
A peculiar kind of dry cough - barking cough that occurs with inflammation of the larynx - laryngitis. A serious complication of this disease can be stenosis of the larynx, or a false croup - a sharp narrowing of the lumen of the upper respiratory tract due to the edema of the mucous membrane lining them.
Sometimes with a cold the children begin to cough in the morning. These short coughs should not cause concern to parents: they arise because the mucus from the nose flows into the respiratory tract, located below.
The organism of a sick child does not receive enough oxygen, which leads to disruption of many metabolic processes. The local immunological defense of the respiratory tract is reduced, and this is fraught with a protracted course of the inflammatory process and may contribute to its chronicization.
Seek immediate medical attention. An in-depth examination of the child is shown.
The regime of a sick child should be gentle, however, it is not necessary to significantly limit the motor activity of a small patient. Movements improve the cleansing of the bronchi from the accumulated mucus, accelerate the recovery.
The main methods of cough treatment in infants with ARVI are measures aimed at liquefaction and removal of sputum.
an increase in a single dose causes nausea and vomiting. In addition, the drugs in this group can significantly increase the amount of sputum that small children can not self-otashljat, which leads to a significant disruption of the drainage function of the bronchi.
Never smoke in the presence of a child!
In winter and spring, babies will have a good 2-3 monthly course of multivitamins with macro and microelements. Often ill children, as well as all children in the period of increased risk of ARVI can recommend the use of herbal products that strengthen the body's defenses.
