The meaning of the name Madina: what does the name mean, what character does it bestow?
We will discuss this below.
One version of the name is its identity with the name of the city of Madinat-en-Nabi, which is located in Medina. This city is considered the cradle of the Prophet Muhammad, has a sacred meaning, and therefore the name of Madina is revered in Muslim countries.
There is also another historical theory of the origin of the name - it can resemble the Magdalena, which is mentioned in the Gospel. It, in turn, went from the name of the settlement on the Sea of Galilee-Magdala.
This name is controlled by a unit, a number that is characteristic of active and motivated people who by any means are accustomed to achieve the goal. She is always the first in solving complex problems, she is not frightened by the difficulties hanging on her, they betray her confidence in her own abilities and in the ability to always come to the aid of friends.
She perfectly prepares, always happy guests. At the same time she has so many acquaintances that she will not disappear in a strange city without a map, she will simply call one of her friends and ask for help.
