Loving parents of great children
In the top of parental inquiries, such qualities of the child as successful, calm, confident, healthy and happy are in the lead. Many believe that without military discipline and obedience, a child will not be able to achieve good results.
All parents have a difficult, busy life, supplemented by a mass of experiences about the upbringing of children. Nevertheless, one of the most important duties of a parent is the ability to stop in time and embrace your children with all the love.
In recent years, there has been more than one scientific study confirming the relationship between parental affection and how happy and successful children will be in adulthood.
The study covered 500 participants, who were observed from infancy up to 30 years. When they were in 8 months, the scientists watched their mother interact with them, and also conducted several development tests.
After 30 years of adults, people were already questioned for their emotional health. Those participants whose mothers were caring or very caring, much less worried about stress and anxiety.
Since the moment you brought the child from the hospital, be sure to hold it on your hands, touch it and rock it in your arms. Try to have a physical contact with him more often (skin to skin).
Finally, be careful not to overdo or "choke" children with your love. Observe their individual level of comfort, and keep in mind that it varies at different stages of development.
