How is pneumonia manifested in adults - the main causes and consequences of improper treatment. Secondary prevention of pneumonia in adults
Pneumonia is a fairly common diagnosis, which causes anxiety and fear in most patients. And not in vain, because untimely diagnosis, lack of treatment leads to serious complications, in the worst case - to death.
Therefore, it is necessary to recognize the first signs of pneumonia in adults and immediately consult a doctor.
The main causes of pneumonia in adults include:
• Viruses. In total, 10-15% pneumonia is of viral origin, most often they occur after ARVI.
An important role is played by risk factors, in which there is a significant increase in the risk of developing the disease.
Symptoms of pneumonia in adults - how not to miss the onset of the disease
• Increased body temperature is a defensive reaction to microbes entering the body. Most often these are high numbers (38.5 ° C and more) that are difficult to treat with antipyretic drugs.
Increased soybean indicates an inflammatory process in the body. If there is leukocytosis, it is most likely a bacterial infection, with an increase in lymphocytes - viral.
• Radiograph of the organs of the chest cavity allows you to see the foci of inflammation in the lungs. Depending on their number, size, location, you can judge the severity of the disease.
An important criterion for the effectiveness of treatment of pneumonia in adults is X-ray dynamics. If the changed areas increase, they become larger, this indicates the need to change the tactics of patient management.
• Additional research methods - CT, MRI of the chest cavity. They are necessary in the presence of complications for differential diagnosis with other diseases.
Treatment of pneumonia in adults is a complex process. Here a lot depends on both the doctor and the patient's readiness to carry out all the necessary recommendations.
• Excessive drinking is the main method of detoxification in patients with mild pneumonia. A large amount of liquid helps to eliminate toxins, decomposition products of bacteria.
• Diet during the period of illness is sparing, enriched with fruits and vegetables. Sweet should be avoided, as it is a good breeding ground for germs.
Efficiency is measured in 2-3 of the day. If the condition has not improved - this is a direct indication to change the group of drugs.
Preventing the disease is much easier than curing it. Therefore, the questions of prevention of pneumonia in adults need to be taken seriously.
1. Strengthening immunity by hardening, walking in the fresh air.
To the points of primary prevention listed above, clinical examination is added, that is, taking into account patients who have suffered pneumonia. They are obliged once a year to do an X-ray of the lungs, after recovery with a periodicity of a month to take a general blood test.
