Celery has a huge amount of nutrients, which makes it so "versatile" in terms of preventing diseases and disorders. It contains several amino acidsthat are difficult to find in other products.
They have anti-inflammatory and antiseptic effects. The benefit can result in harm if the vegetable is consumed excessively or if there is an allergy.
The presence of such a number of useful substances, in particular esters, vitamins, organic components, allows celery to be recommended for diabetics and patients with obesity. In small amounts, celery helps reduce the load on the nervous system.
When used in reasonable amounts, celery will not cause harm. However, there is always such a risk.
Celery juice increases the acidity of gastric juice. Hence the risks of gastritis, stomach ulcers and the initial sections of the small intestine.
Celery damage is also observed due to its ability increase blood coagulation. What can result in thrombosis, thrombophlebitis in some categories of people, or at least, jumps in blood pressure, the formation of varicose veins.
Despite the fact that the vegetable is recommended for losing weight, certain combinations put an end to the potential of celery to burn fat. It is strictly forbidden to consume it with fatty meats, a large amount of oil.
There are no strict contraindications, but some people should use the vegetable carefully. These include:
Hypertensive. Patients with severe cardiovascular disease, in the sub- and decompensated phase.
Pathology of veins, violation of the rheological properties of blood. Possible provocation of thrombosis.
So, vitamin C is destroyed by high temperatures. On the other hand, the juice of the vegetable is neutralized, so baked, boiled celery can be eaten by patients with gastrointestinal diseases.
