Plants well tolerate the winter, and planting irises in the open the soil does not cause trouble. But the peculiarities of growing are worth knowing.
The entire procedure should be done correctly, so that there are no problems with breeding. 1.
2. The iris tubers purchased in the store or at the exhibition are treated as a growth stimulant.
For a full flowering plant needs a superficial planting, so the roots are covered halfway. Deep landing leads to the fact that the irises do not bloom.
Planted in spring, irises bloom for the next year. If the plant releases a flower arrow in the current year, then it must be removed in order not to weaken the flower.
For regular flowering and successful breeding of irises, it is important to consider not only the time of planting, but also to choose the right place. Irises should be planted on an elevated place, where the morning sun will warm their roots.
Reproduction of irises when planting in open ground
In order to reproduce successfully, choose a well-grown healthy bush of iris, dig it out and begin to divide. 1.
Each separate plot must have a leaf bud and one or two tubers. Old roots are pruned, and the damaged tubers are thrown away.
Germs will not have time to take root and die in winter. In this case, the planting of rhizomes is carried out in boxes that are stored at a temperature of 7-8 C throughout the winter.
Care for irises includes standard procedures: weed removal, watering and top dressing. Weeds must be cleaned regularly, but manually, so as not to injure the rhizomes.
Irises are fed from early spring to the second half of summer. The first fertilizing is carried out on moist soil with a granulated fertilizer, which is carefully closed into the soil, trying not to damage the roots.
2. Mineral fertilizers with nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium in the ratio 3: 1: 3 during the budding period.
If nutrients are not enough, irises do not grow well, their flowering is meager. Feeding perennial in the first year after planting is not necessary if the holes were filled by all the rules.
This indicates an incorrect agricultural technique and insufficient maintenance of the plant. Carefully inspect the place where the irises are planted, perhaps it does not comply with the rules.
