Medications, meditation, yoga and sports help against pathological fears and depressive disorders
People with health problems often suffer from anxiety and depressive disorders.
Conversational therapy, medications, and lifestyle changes can help patients.
A new study has now produced some interesting results. People in North America and Western Europe appear to be more prone to depression than people in other parts of the world.
Medications, meditation, yoga and sports help against pathological fears and depressive disorders Fear is important and should not be suppressed or ignored.
However, there are treatment methods, including psychological and medical, that help people improve mental health. These include, for example, physical activity, meditation and yoga.
Then they focused on 48 research. The data showed that from 1990 to 2010, the total number of people with depression remained approximately the same.
The study also showed that about 10% of men and women under the age of 35 are depressed. It is not known why women are more prone to depression.
It is very likely that men are less likely to seek professional help in case of mental health problems. Why young people are more likely to develop fears is not yet known.
In the US, anxiety and depressive disorders cost 42 billion dollars a year. Experts explain that over 60 million people in the EU are also suffering from anxiety disorders.
In Western countries, there is primarily social fear. Experts say that people are always concerned about meeting standards.
In case of chronic anxiety or depression, it is recommended in all cases to seek the advice of a doctor. It is strictly forbidden to engage in self-medication.
