Do athletes really age more slowly than others?
Although sport is important, a healthy diet should not be underestimated.
Sport has a positive effect on a person - improves strength, endurance, mental well-being and overall quality of life. Recently, scientists have discovered that regular physical activity slows down the aging process.
A long-term study showed that people who are quite active in sports remain in all aspects. Athletic people younger than 10 years in motor terms, compared with sedentary people.
Specialists have studied 25 residents of Bad Schönborn for about 500 years, analyzing the exact impact of regular sports on their health.
Scientists at the Sports Institute have so far studied 5 of various parameters to evaluate the positive effects of sports. Test parameters included strength, flexibility, endurance, and fine motor skills.
People who do not play sports are four times more likely to suffer from type 2 diabetes.
However, less than half of all participating volunteers did not even go in for sports for 2 hours a week. The World Health Organization (WHO) recommends that people exercise properly.
Researchers at the Institute for Sports and Sports Science Karlsruhe also explained that exposure to physical activity generally strengthens the body. Such people cope better with stress and have a better overall quality of life.
Experts were especially interested in the impact of sporting events on the health of participants. The study did not address the effects of diet because it would distort the results of the study, experts say.
If a person moves too little and takes a lot of calories, fats and carbohydrates, the body creates reserves. Overweight significantly overloads the cardiovascular system.
The touching babble of a neighbor's baby often causes a slight feeling of envy and anxiety in some mothers, because her child has difficulty mastering the first words and is not in a hurry to enter into intimate conversations with her parents. Maybe something is wrong with the crumb and it's time to go to a specialist?
However, very soon, during a brief wakefulness, he begins to react to light, sound and focus his eyes on his mother. The next two months are characterized by closer acquaintance and communication - at the sight of the native person the crumb smiles, rejoices soundfully, and in 2-3 months begins to "walk" - at first the jerky sounds become more lingering and melodic.
Speech development of the child is successfully continuing - viscous vowel sounds smoothly pass into each other, gradually they begin to add consonants. Kroha tries to imitate Mom and Dad and pleases with the first syllables - pa-pa-pa, yes-yes-yes.
There are dialogues between him and his parents, in which the crumb tries to repeat the words addressed to him, not really thinking about their meaning. At times he stops his babbling, watching my mother's reaction, and, with even more enthusiasm, continues the conversation.
Clearly pronounced vowels and consonants are more successfully combined together, new words appear, consisting mainly of identical syllables - a woman, uncle, kaka. The kid understands about two dozen words, diligently repeating new combinations.
