Therefore, inflammatory and non-inflammatory diseases of certain organs are necessarily manifested by changes in the appearance of the tongue, and the Asians assert that the language starts signaling about a possible illness about a day or two before the affected organs begin to hurt. The best time for diagnosis is in the morning on an empty stomach.
Language purple says a serious pathology of the heart and lungs, but the frighteningly black language is a sign of cholera.
Deep prints of teeth on the front and side of the tongue indicate stress, neurosis or severe fatigue. In addition, fingerprints in the tongue testify to the problems of the digestive tract: dysbacteriosis, slagging and insufficient digestibility of the intestine.
Peptic ulcer of the stomach and duodenum is always accompanied by chronic gastroenteritis, therefore gray coating in the language - an unchanging companion of these diseases.
